---
title: Install Packages
order: 1
description: -S, -U, --needed, --asdeps, install from file
tags: [pacman, install, sync]
---

Installing packages from repositories and local files.

@code bash
# ---- install from repositories (-S) ----

pacman -S package                         # install package
pacman -S package1 package2               # install multiple
pacman -S --needed package                # skip if already installed & up to date
pacman -S extra/package                   # install from specific repo
pacman -S --asdeps package                # install as dependency (not explicit)

# install a package group
pacman -S base-devel                      # prompted to select members
pacman -S --needed base-devel             # skip already-installed members

# answer yes to all prompts
pacman -S --noconfirm package             # skip confirmation

@code bash
# ---- install from file (-U) ----

pacman -U /path/to/package-1.0-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst     # local file
pacman -U https://example.com/package.pkg.tar.zst         # from URL

# install and mark as dependency
pacman -U --asdeps /path/to/package.pkg.tar.zst

@code bash
# ---- overwrite conflicting files ----

# when a file conflict blocks installation
pacman -S package --overwrite '/path/to/conflicting/file'
pacman -S package --overwrite '/usr/lib/python*/site-packages/*'

@code bash
# ---- change install reason ----

# mark package as explicitly installed
pacman -D --asexplicit package

# mark package as dependency
pacman -D --asdeps package

@text
Best practices:
- Always run `pacman -Syu` before installing new packages. Installing
  against a stale sync database risks partial upgrades.
- Use `--needed` when scripting installs to avoid reinstalling packages.
- Use `--asdeps` for packages you only need as build dependencies.
